## What this predicate means

**A `has-end` B** — memorial A is an occurrent (session log, memoir, plan transition, authorization event) and B is its temporal terminating boundary.  The OWL-Time interval-boundary axis applied to occurrent memorials.  Companion to `has-beginning`.  Functional — one end per occurrent (though ongoing occurrents may omit the assertion until they close).

## Substrate identity

- **Slot ident**: `{{predicate-ident}}`
- **Domain**: `{{domain}}`
- **Range**: `{{range}}`
- **Cardinality**: `{{cardinality}}`
- **`:dt/type`**: `:dt/AsymmetricFunctionalIrreflexiveProperty`

## Formal signature

`{{predicate-name}} : {{domain}} × {{range}} → Bool`

## Characteristics

- **Functional** — one end per occurrent (OWL 2 RL `prp-fp`)
- **Asymmetric** — A has-end B doesn't imply B has-end A (OWL 2 RL `prp-asyp`)
- **Irreflexive** — an occurrent isn't its own end (OWL 2 RL `prp-irp`)

## When to use has-end

Use `has-end` for occurrent memorials AFTER they conclude:

- Closed session logs — when did the session end?
- Completed memoirs — when did the recounted period end?
- Resolved plans — when did the plan transition to terminal state?
- Expired authorizations — when did the authorization lapse?

Ongoing occurrents may omit `has-end` (the absence semantically means "still open"); a closing event triggers the assertion.

